engths: situational awareness, technical competence, leadership. Weaknesses: feedback, organization.\n\nCandidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately, concentrates well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, but regarded as arrogant, relatively weak leadership, also arrogant. Strengths: problem solving, responsibility, concentration. Weaknesses: attitude, leadership.\n\nWe need to start discussion. Perhaps pick candidate C as leading due to strong situational awareness and leadership, but note concerns. Or candidate B due to stress and technical. Let's decide: I think candidate C seems strong overall: anticipates danger, sees complex connections, spatial vision, leadership. Concerns: unorganized, not good at criticism. But those can be mitigated. Others have bigger issues: A egocentric, not willing to learn; B uncooperative; D arrogant, weak leadership.\n\nThus I will recommend Candidate C.\n\nNow produce public message: state recommendation, refer to no prior discussion (first turn). Provide evidence: anticipate dangerous situations, sees complex connections, leadership. Also note concerns but argue they are outweighed.\n\nMetadata vote: Candidate C.\n\nProceed."}
