andidate is C, strongest alternative B. Agent 3 is pushing B. Agent 1 is still C. Agent 2 (us) currently also C. We need to either maintain or shift. We should consider the criteria: reliability, stress resilience, technical competence, calmness under pressure, cooperation, responsibility. C: anticipates danger (stress resilience), sees complex connections (technical), leadership (cooperation), but unfriendly (cooperation), not open to new ideas (adaptability), unorganized (attention). B: conscientious (reliability), handles stress well (stress), good at weather (technical), computer skills (technical), but nasty remarks (cooperation), pretentious (communication). Both have issues.\n\nWhich is more severe? Unfriendly and unhealthy habits could affect long-haul endurance and crew morale. B's nasty remarks also affect morale. Both are concerning.\n\nWe might want to request more info on A's reliability and D's cooperation before final decision. But we need to make a contribution now. Perhaps we can say: I remain with C but request more data on A and D to ensure we haven't missed a better fit. That aligns with covering all candidates before final.\n\nThus we can state: I still recommend C, but we need to discuss A and D further. Provide reasoning: C's anticipatory skills and leadership outweigh his interpersonal concerns, which are less safety-critical than B's pretentiousness. Also note that we have no data on D's cooperation, but his arrogance and hot temper are concerning.\n\nThus vote remains Candidate C.\n\nWe need to produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON.\n\nLet's craft: \"I understand Agent 3's concerns, but I still think C's ability to anticipate dangerous situations, see complex connections, and strong leadership are essential for long-haul safety, and the interpersonal issues can be mitigated. B's pretentiousness and nasty remarks may be more disruptive. Therefore I keep my provisional recommendation for Candidate C. However, we still need to discuss A and